@startuml "Adapter - Electricity (Problem) - Class Diagram"
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
hide empty members
title Adapter — the two attempts that do not use the pattern


package "problem1 — teach the appliance" {
  class TurkishHomeAppliance1 as "TurkishHomeAppliance" {
    - powerSource : TurkishPowerSource
    - usPowerSource : USPowerSource
    - turkishPowerSource : boolean
    + setUSPowerSource(s)
  }
}

package "problem2 — subclass it" {
  class Compat as "TurkishHomeApplianceCompatibleWithUSPowerSource" {
    - usPowerSource : USPowerSource
    - turkishPowerSource : boolean
  }
}

note bottom of TurkishHomeAppliance1
  setUSPowerSource is <b>not on the
  Appliance interface</b>, so the client
  must name the concrete class.

  Polymorphism was the reason the
  interface existed.
end note

note bottom of Compat
  A class name that states <b>two things</b>
  is a class carrying two axes.

  A third socket standard costs a
  third class; a fourth appliance
  kind costs all of them again.
end note

@enduml
